      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To the chief Musician, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "A Psalm",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of David. The fool hath said in his heart, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "There is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no God. They are corrupt, they have done abominable works, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " none that doeth good.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.14.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.14.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The LORD looked down from heaven upon the children of men, to see if there were any that did understand, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " seek God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.14.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.14.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They are all gone aside, they are ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "all",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " together become filthy: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " none that doeth good, no, not one.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.14.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.14.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Have all the workers of iniquity no knowledge? who eat up my people ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they eat bread, and call not upon the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.14.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.14.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There were they in great fear: for God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the generation of the righteous.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.14.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.14.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye have shamed the counsel of the poor, because the LORD ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his refuge.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.14.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.14.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oh that the salvation of Israel ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were come",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " out of Zion! when the LORD bringeth back the captivity of his people, Jacob shall rejoice, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Israel shall be glad.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
